QtRocket is a C++ re-implementation of OpenRocket (https://openrocket.info), Copyright (C) 2007-2025 Sampo
Niskanen and others, licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later. The component model,
aerodynamic and mass calculations, simulation engine and the .ork file format follow OpenRocket's design and
algorithms. The bundled motor database (data/motors/initial_motors.db, with its version in
data/motors/metadata.json), example designs (data/examples/) and legacy component presets
(data/components/internal/) are taken from OpenRocket unchanged. The designs of older
file format versions that the tests read (tests/data/ork/) are example and test designs of OpenRocket's releases
0.9.3 to 23.09, copied unchanged from its repository; tests/data/ork/README.md lists the release and the path of
each. The reference data the tests compare with (tests/data/goldens/, tests/data/component-factory/,
tests/data/fin-images/report.txt and the tables that name a generator) is OpenRocket's output, written by the Java
programs in tools/, which run OpenRocket's compiled classes. Where those programs cannot run a part of OpenRocket
as it is, they contain its code adapted line for line (tools/openrocket-gui-reference/: OpenRocket's GUI actions;
tools/openrocket-goldens/: the geometry of its rocket figure), each place naming its source: part of OpenRocket,
GPL version 3 or later, as above.


